# Normalize line endings to LF for all text files, regardless of the checkout platform's
# core.autocrlf. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true, the Git-for-Windows
# default) converts every file to CRLF on disk while biome.jsonc's formatter.lineEnding is "lf",
# so a repo-wide `bun run lint` (the pre-commit hook's first step) fails on every file the
# working tree hasn't been through `biome format` on since the last checkout — hundreds of files
# with no content change of their own. This declares the repository's own norm (LF), independent
# of any one clone's local git config, which this project never modifies programmatically.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuinely binary — never touched by line-ending normalization.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
